      "id": 18653,
      "name": "MindWanderer",
      "username": "MindWanderer",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/mindwanderer/{size}/4816_2.png",
      "created_at": "2018-10-17T18:17:35.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>So... Super Sentai Idealist and Completionist Guise.&nbsp; Both put cards under their character card, but with very different assumptions.</p>\n<p>What happens if Completionist Guise has character cards under himself and uses I Can Do That Too to Form the Head?&nbsp; He should be able to destroy a character card.&nbsp; If he does, where does it go?&nbsp; Even more humorously, what if the villain is Challenge mode Chokepoint?</p>\n<p>Fortunately, it looks like if Super Sentai Idealist uses Called to Judgement or Character Witnesses to try to form her own&nbsp;Impressive Collection, the collected cards go under Guise and not Idealist.&nbsp; However, it does raise the question of where those character cards go when Representative of Earth is destroyed (and whether this triggers destruction effects).</p>",
      "post_number": 1,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:52:04.902Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
      "quote_count": 0,
      "incoming_link_count": 9,
      "reads": 1,
      "readers_count": 0,
      "score": 45.2,
      "yours": false,
      "topic_id": 18652,
      "topic_slug": "completionist-guise-destroys-his-collection",
